/**
 * C1: TAKING PART (docs/43-lessons.md §15.3, part 6).
 *
 * Late spring of the family's third year, in the district they moved to in the
 * winter. The city wants to rebuild their street: one lane for cars, a bike
 * path, wider pavements, sixty trees and forty parking places fewer. The part
 * follows the plan from the morning show to the public hearing: the item on
 * the radio, the consultation Helgi explains, a radio debate before the local
 * election, a volunteer day in the park by the street, a piece for the
 * district paper, and the hearing where Urve, the city planner, presents it.
 *
 * One pattern is explained here and nowhere else in the level: a whole case
 * (`argument`, lesson 31), the claim, two points developed, the other side's
 * best case put fairly and the answer to it, held together by {iseenesest},
 * {teisalt}, {õigupoolest} and {kokkuvõttes}. The part writes the paper's
 * opinion text, 220 to 260 words on two given points, and ends on the hearing,
 * where the move is summing up both sides before you answer (§15.5).
 *
 * Who is who is `docs/reviews/c1-cast.md`. Strangers each used in one lesson
 * only: the two council candidates on the radio, Pille and Toivo (lesson 33);
 * the morning show's guest on volunteering, Kaarel (lesson 34); and Arvo, the
 * neighbor at the hearing who gets the figures wrong (lesson 36).
 *
 * In preview (`preview.ts`) until C1 is the course, and held to every check a
 * lesson is (`npx tsx scripts/check-lesson-part.ts --part c1-uhiskond`).
 */

